            "vd_help_heading|The Disk manager",
            "vd_help_intro|Every virtual disk FileDO knows about is one row: the disks in your list, the ones mounted now and the disk images FileDO mounted. A virtual disk is one .fdd file that Windows shows as a drive - mount it to use the drive, unmount it when you are done, and the file keeps everything. A partition disk is the same, kept in a new partition in free space on a GPT disk instead of a file (not in the Microsoft Store version).",
