            "vd_auto_switch_on_text|At every logon a watcher starts, hidden, and at the end of your session it saves dirty ram disks and unmounts every mounted container. Creating the task asks for administrator consent once. Uninstalling FileDO does not remove the task: take the guard off here, or with filedo vd guard off.",
            "vd_auto_switch_off_title|Turn the shutdown guard off?",
            "vd_auto_switch_off_text|The task is removed and no disk is touched. Mounted containers stay mounted; the session's end is simply not tidied, so the next logon reports every container as not closed cleanly.",
            "vd_auto_note_consent|The guard's task runs with administrator rights, because unmounting needs them; creating it asks for consent once, and every logon after that is silent.",
